{"id": "sevt_01FgEkkpZWYA8CoZf84S7Kyb", "content": [{"text": "**No, auth isn't the problem.** The checkout deploy `a3f9c21` is.\n\n**Evidence**\n- **Timing:** Checkout p99 went from about 75 ms to about 3,860 ms at 14:31. The checkout deploy `a3f9c21` landed at 14:31:18, so the gap is about zero. Latency has kept climbing since, to about 4.9 s by 14:59.\n- **Diff:** The commit is described as a readability refactor. It replaces one batched `order_items WHERE order_id IN (...)` query with a loop that runs one query per open order. That is an N+1.\n- **Log:** The batched query appears 137 times, all before the deploy. The per-row query `... WHERE order_id = ?` appears 3,320 times, starting at 14:31:18.496 on checkout-3, the same second as the deploy.\n- **Knock-on effects:**\n  - Checkout `db_pool_utilization` climbs from about 0.15 to 1.0 between 14:31 and 14:40 and stays pinned.\n  - Checkout `error_rate` starts at 14:40, the minute the pool saturates.\n  - The log has 70 \"pool exhausted\" lines and shows active=50/50 connections.\n- **Auth is clean:**\n  - Auth p99 stays flat at about 50\u201380 ms through the whole window.\n  - The auth deploy `9f1e2d4` landed at 11:02, hours before the incident.\n  - Auth logged 6 identity-provider timeouts and some minor GC pauses. The timeouts I looked at were around 14:15, before the incident, so they don't line up with it.\n- **Other deploys:** The inventory deploy `7b3e8f0` at 14:55 came after the latency jump, so it can't be the trigger. The cart deploy was at 09:14, also too early.\n\n**Mitigation:** Roll back `a3f9c21`, or restore the batched query with `order_id__in`. A rollback should also clear the pool saturation and the errors.\n\n> **Root cause:** `a3f9c21` \u2014 the \"readability\" refactor of `CheckoutSummaryHandler.build_summary` turned one batched `order_items` query into one query per order. That multiplied DB round-trips, saturated checkout's 50-connection pool (`pool exhausted`), and drove p99 from about 75 ms to over 4 s.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T06:00:45.697844Z", "type": "agent.message"}
